<dashboard version="1.1" theme="dark">
  <label>Lab Info</label>
  <description>What this lab is, how it is built, and where the code lives.</description>

  <row>
    <panel>
      <html>
        <h1>Splunk Location-Based RBAC Lab</h1>
        <p>
          A self-rebuilding Splunk lab for Cisco dCloud. The environment resets to an
          empty template each session, so on every startup a script pulls this project
          from GitHub and re-creates the full configuration from scratch: per-location
          indexes, RBAC roles, users, and dashboards. Nothing here is configured by
          hand - it is all code, so the lab is identical every time.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b>Repository:</b>
          <a href="https://github.com/js-csco/splunk-dcloud" target="_blank">github.com/js-csco/splunk-dcloud</a>
        </p>
        <h3>What gets pre-loaded on each session</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>6 indexes</b>, one namespace per location: <code>loc1_*</code>, <code>loc2_*</code>, <code>loc3_*</code></li>
          <li><b>3 RBAC roles</b>: <code>role_loc1</code> (loc1 only), <code>role_loc2</code> (loc2 only), <code>role_global</code> (all)</li>
          <li><b>3 users</b>: <code>user_loc1</code>, <code>user_loc2</code>, <code>user_global</code></li>
          <li><b>Dashboards</b>: Lab Info (this page), Setup Status, Ingestion &amp; Health</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Start here, then open <b>Setup Status</b> to confirm everything loaded correctly
          before the demo begins.
        </p>
      </html>
    </panel>
  </row>

