  <row>
    <panel>
      <title>Splunk environment</title>
      <table>
        <search>
          <query>| rest /services/server/info | eval uptime_hours=round(startup_time_delta/3600,1) | rename version as Version, build as Build, os_name as OS, cpu_arch as Arch, numberOfCores as Cores, serverName as Host, uptime_hours as "Uptime (h)" | table Version Build OS Arch Cores Host "Uptime (h)"</query>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">none</option>
      </table>
    </panel>
    <panel>
      <title>How this lab is deployed</title>
      <html>
        <p>On each session start, dCloud Startup Automation runs one command that fixes DNS,
        clones this repo, and applies the config:</p>
        <pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-all;background:#11151a;padding:10px;border-radius:6px;">git clone -b main https://github.com/js-csco/splunk-dcloud.git /opt/dcloud-splunk &amp;&amp; bash /opt/dcloud-splunk/apply.sh</pre>
        <p style="color:#8b98a5;">To change the lab, edit the repo and push to <code>main</code> - the next
        session picks it up automatically.</p>
      </html>
    </panel>
  </row>
